WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:01.667
 Caleb.

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:02.401
Forrest.

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:03.803
Congratulations.

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:04.670
You guys have made it
into the final round

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:05.972
of this competition.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.940
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.744
to recreate this iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.414
The sword of Goujian.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.017
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:19.352
We will see you in four days.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:20.019
 Don't worry, man.

00:00:20.085 --> 00:00:22.655 line:14%
 Congratulations.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:25.391 line:8%
 We're going to take on
the sword of Goujian today.

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:28.761
I'm gonna started at the
tip, work back to the tang.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.164
I'm keeping the blade
rather thick, because I just

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.132
don't want to mess
with any twisting

00:00:33.198 --> 00:00:34.667
and bending once it quenches.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.470
I am surprised how fast
this is coming along.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.172
So far, so good.

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:43.876
Now it's time to get the
blade hot so I can quench it.

00:00:43.976 --> 00:00:45.244
I'm happy.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:46.979
I think we have a little
work in it here and there,

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:49.716
but nothing the grinder
won't take care of.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:56.322 line:8%
 Today, I have to get
started on my sword.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:01:00.326
I'm bringing these new school
vibes to this really old school

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:01.594
weapon.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.229
Instead of bronze, I'm
bringing Damascus to the table.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.631
Hopefully, this
will just give me

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.534
a really, really cool
contrast with the pattern

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:08.867
whenever I'm done with it.

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:10.870
All the welds are set good.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.772
I'm getting the
metal drawn out good.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.207
A nice, square bar.

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:17.977
And from there, I'm trying
to go for a twist pattern.

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:19.879
I want quite a few
good twists in there,

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:22.048
a pretty tight pattern.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:22.848
All right.

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:24.416
That'll do.

00:01:24.516 --> 00:01:27.052
The end of day one,
it's still not a weapon.

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:29.289
But it's getting there.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.294
 Today, I'm hoping to
have my guard fitted on.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:38.098
Maybe even the handle.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:41.734
For my guard, I'm going to
use a piece of angle iron.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.069
The guard's around it, over now.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.837
I'm just going to put a
hole through the bottom

00:01:44.937 --> 00:01:46.405
just to go over the tang.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:47.774
[groans]

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.276
The guard actually split.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.244
Cracked.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.811
All that fun for nothing.

00:01:52.878 --> 00:01:54.814
So I have to start over.

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.482
I have a pile of
railroad spikes.

00:01:56.582 --> 00:02:00.153
That would be putting the new
school into the bronze metal,

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:01.855
old school sword.

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:07.226
Fits on the tang really nice.

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:10.562 line:8%
But there's more
work to be done.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:14.333 line:8%
 The plan for today is
to get to work on actually

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.768
forging out the sword.

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:17.370
My goal for the
end of the day is

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:19.005
definitely to get it quenched.

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.639
This thing's getting long.

00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:22.608
Just trying to keep it
where it's not too thin,

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:25.512
so that when I quench
it, everything goes well.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:26.746
We're about ready.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.415
I'm really just hoping that
nothing goes wrong here.

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:32.552
This is the most important
step of the entire process.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:37.723
It's pretty straight.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:38.858
Excited with the quench.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:41.059 line:14%
It went well.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.564 line:8%
 Morning of day
3, and I'm tired.

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:47.199
First thing today, I'm going
to make my blade lighter.

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:48.868
Right now, the
balance is about five

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.036
inches in front of the guard.

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:51.704
I would like it to
be-- within an inch

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:53.038
or two would make me happy.

00:02:53.138 --> 00:02:55.241
It's starting to feel lighter.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.377
But I have a lot
more grinding to go.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:04.550
OK.

00:03:04.616 --> 00:03:08.221
I start grinding on my edge,
and my belt sander just quits.

00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:09.322
Flip the breaker.

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.560
I'm not sure what
I'm going to do.

00:03:16.628 --> 00:03:18.965
I've decided to go grab
two extension cords

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:22.135
and run power from
the house to the shop.

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:24.570
We got-- we got power
somewhere else we can use.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.973
I plug the belt sander
into the house power.

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:32.445
And it works.

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:35.481
Hopefully, now I can get
the edge on the blade.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:38.451
My blade's looking fine
and just needs a little

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:40.453
more sharpening and polishing.

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:44.757 line:8%
 Finally starting to see that
light at the end of the tunnel

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.125
now.

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:48.427
First thing, I'm going to
start on my disc pommel.

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:50.196
I'm just going to take
this piece of just normal,

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:52.498
mild steel, chop it off,
and kind of try to forge

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:55.434
it into a bit of a disc shape.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.736
I'm kind of at a
square right now,

00:03:56.802 --> 00:04:00.240
and I'm looking more
or less for a circle.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.508
I'm just going to kind of
grind and polish off the top

00:04:02.608 --> 00:04:05.177
and make it into a truer circle.

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:06.612
Time's running out.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:10.449
I need to sharpen my blade,
and then finally finish

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:11.917
and put together the sword.

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:13.486
It's a little twisted.

00:04:16.588 --> 00:04:18.691
The handle on the
blade is centered,

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.693
and it looks centered,
but on the inside,

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.463
as you can see right here,
it's not perfectly centered.

00:04:24.563 --> 00:04:27.099
But of course, with
a pin and epoxy

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.300
and a disc and
scroll in the back,

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:30.603
it's going to be
very, very strong.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:33.071
Forrest really better
bring it, because if not,

00:04:33.138 --> 00:04:34.507
I'm going to chop him down.

00:04:36.675 --> 00:04:41.080
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.514
To find out what
kind of lethal damage

00:04:42.614 --> 00:04:44.917
your weapon will do according
to its historic design,

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:46.419
I will take your
weapon and deliver

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.320
some killing thrusts and blows
on this ballistics dummy.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:49.655
Forrest, are you up for this?

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:50.222
 Yes, sir.

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:51.824
 Let's do this.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:55.428
[dramatic music]

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:21.654
All right, Forrest.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:22.855
Let's talk about
your weapon here.

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:25.257
And it's very forward heavy.

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:27.226
What makes it hard
to handle is the fact

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:29.928
that you have a very
skinny handle right here.

00:05:29.995 --> 00:05:32.832
A lot of these movements,
your blade went up on contact

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:34.533
and was spinning in my hand.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.469
I had to adjust several
times to make sure that I

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:39.405
stayed on the edge over here.

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.407
Now, the edge is sharp.

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:44.477
Once it makes contact and
you slash, it digs deep.

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:48.447
Overall, sir, it'll kill.

00:05:48.547 --> 00:05:49.749
All right, Caleb.
You're up.

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:50.750
You ready?

00:05:50.817 --> 00:05:52.284
 Let's see it.

00:05:52.351 --> 00:05:55.888
[dramatic music]

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:21.914
 All right, Caleb.

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:26.352
First up, the blade in
itself, balance-wise, I

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:27.620
think you nailed it.

00:06:27.686 --> 00:06:29.288
Now, your handle construction.

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:30.556
It's ovoid.

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:32.024
It's actually comfortable.

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:36.228
Because of the balance
and a very sharp edge,

00:06:36.328 --> 00:06:38.130
all the cuts are
very, very deep.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:42.735
Overall, sir, it'll kill.

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:47.006
 Bladesmiths, welcome to the
strength test, the gong chop.

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:49.341
To test the strength and
durability of your edges,

00:06:49.408 --> 00:06:50.709
as well as the
overall construction

00:06:50.776 --> 00:06:52.645
of your swords of
Goujian, I'm going to be

00:06:52.711 --> 00:06:54.280
chopping them into these gongs.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:55.180
Forrest, you're up first.

00:06:55.247 --> 00:06:55.948
You ready?

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:56.849
 Yes, sir.

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:59.952
[dramatic music]

00:07:18.137 --> 00:07:21.640
Well, Forrest, your sword did
take some damage on the edge.

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:25.110
There's some rolls sort
of crushed in right here.

00:07:25.177 --> 00:07:27.647
Your handle is really small.

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:29.949
A bigger handle would've helped
me control this really well.

00:07:30.049 --> 00:07:33.419
But all that being said, that
much damage in a big strength

00:07:33.486 --> 00:07:35.087
test like this?

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:36.354
Well done.

00:07:36.421 --> 00:07:37.589
 Thank you.

00:07:37.656 --> 00:07:38.858
 All right, Caleb.
You're up.

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:39.425
You ready?

00:07:39.492 --> 00:07:40.392
 Heck yeah, man.

00:07:40.493 --> 00:07:43.663
[dramatic music]

00:07:59.946 --> 00:08:00.913
 Well, Caleb.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.247
You did a great job
with the Damascus.

00:08:02.348 --> 00:08:04.015
I love to see this
kind of stuff.

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:05.685
It's beautiful.

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:09.421
Your blade is still straight,
true, and the weight on this

00:08:09.488 --> 00:08:11.523
is phenomenal.

00:08:11.623 --> 00:08:14.292
There is one big issue, though.

00:08:14.359 --> 00:08:15.894
Your handle.

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:18.397
It's loose now.

00:08:18.464 --> 00:08:21.032
Your handle is coming apart.

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:22.068
I can move it.

00:08:22.134 --> 00:08:24.136
And the pommel is also loose.

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:26.872
If these were right and
tight and held in place,

00:08:26.972 --> 00:08:29.041
then it tends to help everything
else stay where it is.

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:31.010
But just a little bit
of play in this guard

00:08:31.076 --> 00:08:33.446
can send shockwaves
right down the handle.

00:08:33.513 --> 00:08:35.081
But I've got to say,
that's one heck of a blade.

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:36.181
- Thank you.
- It's just--

00:08:36.248 --> 00:08:37.750
 Thank you.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:39.017
 You know, this handle that's
really causing the issue now.

00:08:39.084 --> 00:08:39.886
 Yes, sir.

00:08:43.855 --> 00:08:47.492
 So we've got a
pretty mobile opening.

00:08:47.559 --> 00:08:50.096
 Then it has a
corresponding split

00:08:50.162 --> 00:08:51.531
on the back side of the handle.

00:08:51.597 --> 00:08:53.799
 Not only is it loose, but
the material that's loose

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:54.634
has sharp edges.

00:08:54.734 --> 00:08:55.200
 OK.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.435
 Yeah.

00:08:56.535 --> 00:08:57.469
I mean, this would
require either taping

00:08:57.536 --> 00:08:58.938
that up, or wearing a glove.

00:08:59.004 --> 00:09:01.173
And now we're not testing
the same as the other one.

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:01.907
 OK.

00:09:02.007 --> 00:09:02.808 line:14%
Ben?

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:07.145 line:14%
 Dave?

00:09:07.245 --> 00:09:07.947
 That one kills me.
Yeah.

00:09:08.014 --> 00:09:08.347
Can't have it.

00:09:08.447 --> 00:09:09.448
 Doug?

00:09:09.515 --> 00:09:10.182
 I agree.

00:09:10.282 --> 00:09:11.284
 All right.

00:09:16.855 --> 00:09:18.623
 Now, we've
continued with blades

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:20.693
that had loose parts before.

00:09:25.731 --> 00:09:29.068
We've continued with blades
that had split handles before.

00:09:29.135 --> 00:09:33.572
 Your handle has cracked.

00:09:33.639 --> 00:09:36.108
 However, the combination
of the two things

00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:39.679
has made your blade unsafe
to continue with any testing.

00:09:39.745 --> 00:09:42.415
And therefore, you cannot be
our "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:42.481 --> 00:09:44.517
I'd like to invite you
to shake our hands,

00:09:44.617 --> 00:09:47.219
shake your competitor's
hand, and then I have to ask

00:09:47.319 --> 00:09:49.855
you to please leave the forge.

00:09:49.921 --> 00:09:51.557
 I can't blame the
judges' decision.

00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:53.425
It's definitely unsafe
to use at this point,

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:54.660
but that's a good call.

00:09:54.727 --> 00:09:56.061
If I could have
done it differently,

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:58.597
probably would have put a
pin or two in my handle.

00:09:58.664 --> 00:10:00.899
Might not have looked
as good, but the use is

00:10:00.999 --> 00:10:02.234
more important than the looks.

00:10:02.334 --> 00:10:03.268
Thank you so much, Forrest.

00:10:03.369 --> 00:10:04.636
I appreciate it.

00:10:04.703 --> 00:10:06.271
I may not be the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:10:06.371 --> 00:10:09.174
but man, I'm walking out of
here with my head held high,

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:10.009
and I'm proud.

00:10:12.444 --> 00:10:14.146
 Forrest, congratulations.

00:10:14.213 --> 00:10:15.848
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:10:15.914 --> 00:10:17.716
and that is a title
that comes with a check

00:10:17.783 --> 00:10:19.318
for $10,000, my friend.

00:10:19.418 --> 00:10:20.018
Good job.

00:10:20.119 --> 00:10:21.620
Come on forward.

00:10:21.686 --> 00:10:23.388
 I'm thrilled that
I'm the champion.

00:10:23.455 --> 00:10:24.957
Hasn't even soaked in yet.

00:10:25.023 --> 00:10:27.792
In the next day or two, I'll
really realize what's happened.

00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:29.361
Being a "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:10:29.427 --> 00:10:32.565
means that I've succeeded in
the goal that I wanted to reach.

00:10:32.632 --> 00:10:34.699
This is for everyone at
home, and I'm coming home

00:10:34.766 --> 00:10:36.301
a "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:10:36.401 --> 00:10:38.037
Yee haw.

